WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.465
They spent fifty years trying to make it look as though I was only ever here by their leave.

00:00:06.315 --> 00:00:07.930
I never gave it to them.

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:15.070
Just sign here, Mr Williams. A monthly tenancy. Eight shillings. A formality.

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:19.570
A tenancy? On ground my family has always worked?

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:21.184
Don't sign it, Dad.

00:00:21.034 --> 00:00:25.900
Once it's on their paper, they'll say we were only ever here on their say-so.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:32.620
He was 72. They leaned on him until he did. That was the first of their papers.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:37.820
Western Ground Rents would like you to take up a fresh agreement.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:42.790
No. My father's agreement died with him. I'll sign nothing.

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:48.459
I want to report our title deeds missing. They were in the house.

00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:49.510
Now they're gone.

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:54.090
The sergeant wrote it all down. The deeds never came back.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:58.519
I came home from the hospital with one leg.

00:00:58.369 --> 00:01:02.010
They were already on my land, both sides of the house.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.580
We have a possession order, madam.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:09.650
Not for this house you haven't. This is my home, and I own it.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.140
Now get off my land.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:17.390
A proper tenancy. A fair rent. It would settle everything.

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:20.530
It would settle it your way. No.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:26.150
One more offer. Sign, and you'll never be troubled again.

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:30.000
Same answer as 1939. No.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:37.530
Then the same men came back in different coats. Western Ground Rents became BP.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:43.780
In 1969 BP bought the land they had seized around me.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:49.638
And they bought something else: an interest in an old order against my home.

00:01:49.488 --> 00:01:53.480
Not the title. An order no one could lawfully enforce.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:02:00.200
My Lord, she holds no title. We ask the court to extinguish her claim.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:04.120
I will not do that. This matter is adjourned.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:09.740
We hold an order from 1962. You are to leave.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.583
That order was never enforceable.

00:02:12.433 --> 00:02:16.498
It rests on the 1955 order, and that was for Parcel B.

00:02:16.348 --> 00:02:19.180
A different piece of land altogether.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.870
What is this place to you?

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:27.920
It's my home. It always has been. And I'm not going anywhere.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:34.400
My client's position is clear. This is her home, and she is staying in it.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:41.690
Then, quietly, out of my sight, BP and my own lawyer shook hands.

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:49.321
It's good news. BP have offered to let you stay. The 1962 order is quashed.

00:02:49.171 --> 00:02:55.700
You're there on licence now, and BP own it. There's nothing more you need to do.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:01.575
Dear Sirs. The 1955 order was for Parcel B, not my home.

00:03:01.425 --> 00:03:07.460
Western Ground Rents should never have taken the land either side of my house.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.894
I know what this is. A racket.

00:03:09.744 --> 00:03:14.986
They draw up one-sided papers to make it look as if I'm here on their say-so.

00:03:14.836 --> 00:03:20.740
Twelve years later they take them to the Land Registry, and register my land as theirs.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.282
The council did it on one side of my house in 1970.

00:03:25.132 --> 00:03:30.739
Cardiff Corporation on the other, in 1961. Twelve years, both times.

00:03:30.589 --> 00:03:34.430
And Parcel B in 1952, twelve years after 1939.

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:41.871
Now BP, twelve years after their order, dress it up as stopping the clock on me, on land I own.

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:45.330
That is beyond white collar crime. It is fraud.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:52.540
In February 1983 BP applied to register my land in their name.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:57.809
They never told the Land Registry I was claiming it. They never told me.

00:03:57.659 --> 00:04:02.160
I died a few weeks later, and only then did my family hear of it.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.500
The plaintiffs are entitled to possession.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:11.780
In 1987 the court gave BP possession of the whole farm.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:19.161
While my son William was still appealing, BP and the Land Registry merged the titles.

00:04:19.011 --> 00:04:21.790
Then they called it all the whole farm.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:27.800
The petition of William Buckler for leave to appeal is refused.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.800
Then they bulldozed the house.

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:39.350
The application is declared inadmissible.

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:44.710
William took it to the European Court of Human Rights. He lost there too.

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:48.974
They're building houses on my mother's farm.

00:04:48.824 --> 00:04:51.350
I'll petition against every one of them.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:57.520
He petitioned until the day he died. He never gave it up. Neither did I.
